  "version": 1,
  "note": "Spec 07 §4.3, as a floor. variables: §4.3's table, then the names the pinned Claude Code reads that change the model, effort, endpoint, credential or settings source, each with its kind. patterns: the families those names come from, so a new variant is refused by default; the first that matches gives the kind. Every CLAUDE* and ANTHROPIC_* name, and every name holding OAUTH, is refused unless allowed or sessionMarkers lists it, because the client adds such names in every release. allowed: names a pattern would catch that the engine needs: the CI federation inputs and session settings of §4.3, and the local credential of §7.3. sessionMarkers: the names Claude Code sets in every command its tools run that only identify the calling session; the engine runs from the agents' sessions (EX-09, §7.1), so they are tolerated in its own environment, and none reaches a review session, whose environment is built from nothing (§4.3). Each must be a name only the client patterns catch, never one that a variables entry or a model, effort, endpoint, credential or settings family covers, except as an object that names the one other family the name is in and says why the client's value cannot change a review. settingsKeys: §4.3's keys and the keys that run commands, load code or change the model, refused in any settings file Claude Code could read; settingsAllowedKeys: the only other top-level keys such a file may hold. An env block is refused whatever it names, and permissions may only narrow §4.2's grant.",
